igure out what happen again on micro  dosing has even allowed him to taper off  his use of adderall micro dosing of  psychedelics LSD specifically has been  something that has allowed me to not  feel trapped in my current ADHD  medication that there's another answer  there's another way to be able to have a  cognitive enhancement the use of  psychedelics as productivity and  creativity hacks reaches back to the  very beginnings of Silicon Valley the  minute that you understand that you can  poke life and actually something will if  you push in something will pop out the  other side you can you can change you  can mold it that's maybe the most  important thing when Steve Jobs told his  biographer taking LSD was a profound  experience one of the most important  things in my life it was bound to have  an impact jobs willingness to speak out  helped inspire Burt to go public people  like Steve Jobs in his public advocacy  certainly is helped but it means people  have to actually step up and state what  they've been doing not just that there  has to be less repercussions from from  the government for for engaging in  activity that's illegal drug prohibition  has prevented scientists from studying  the effects of microtubule SD that  started to change migrate was originated  because Albert Hofmann who originated  LSD had tried of course all kinds of  doses in his lifetime and he actually  micro dosed for many years himself he  said it helped him think about his  thinking and he indicated this was an  under research area and I became  interested because it wasn't under  research area James Fadiman is an author  and researcher at sofa University in  Palo Alto  and he's gathering survey data from LSD  micro dosers about their experiences  what we've done is what I call search  which is here's some uses of  psychedelics that we don't really know  about a really understand all we seem to  know is that they're they matter to  people and they're very safe so we've  basically said to people we can suggest  how you can take it safely and  effectively in return you tell us how  it's working for you both with physical  conditions mental conditions and for  enhanced health people who are either  depressed or on antidepressants and  don't like it find that micro dosing in  many many cases turns around their  depression very very quickly  another area are people who are in the  creative arts or in the creative science  more who find that they function a  little better meaning they can basically  work slightly not necessarily more  creative but more time in in what's  called flow Fadiman isn't making any  empirical claims his hope is that  scientists will use his observations as  a starting point for further research  it's as if we've now discovered this new  world and we've mapped it a little bit  and now someone says well now let's get  the hard science under this and what I  hear from the research community is  they're ready to go George Burke hopes  that micro dosing will continue catching  on in Silicon Valley and Beyond with a  population of 300 million in the United  States imagine 1 percent of those people  are taking some form of cognitive  enhancer it's 3 million people who would  be able to solve problems better and  faster and with a better sense of  connectedness than we haven't seen  before what impact would that have on  America  I can't imagine but I think it would be  I think would be profound  [Music]  [Music]
 

